+order, empirical attribution}\label{sec:d210}
+
+The v0.18.0 limitations named the shared kit and the asymmetric formats
+as a construct threat; the extension plan (D210) was pre-registered to
+close it, its hash consigned before any measurement
+(\code{4a3b1311\ldots}): $n\ge6$ fully instrumented units (the four
+tasks not yet instrumented --- loupe-02 LIRE, loupe-08 LIGNE, loupe-13
+RECHERCHE, loupe-16 SAISIE --- joining the two earlier pairs at
+$n{=}1$ and $n{=}2$), identical formats across arms (every piece
+delivered at both the sealed EXE slot and the loader-bound DLL: the
+unbound-leaf class re-tested on both loading paths), the arm order
+randomized per unit (the seed 20261117 consigned before the first
+call; the public draw gave the T arm first in all four units --- a
+one-in-eight event, consigned as drawn, never re-drawn), the D207 stop
+rule reconducted, and the empirical attribution test: the fourth
+unit's C piece re-delivered through a minimal standard kit, the
+question ``would the pure compiled flow have produced the escapes?''
+tranch\'ee on pieces. Three directional hypotheses were registered
+with the plan: H6 (the kit-side escape rate within a factor of two
+between arms at identical formats --- the replication of H2), H7 (the
+randomized order affects no metric at the 5\% threshold --- the order
+test), H8 (the corrective spiral remains the hot path of both arms:
+above 50\% of each unit's tokens). The four metrics are the
+campaign's own (M1 under the D202 rule, M2 real tokens read from
+usage logs, M3 the developer's human time at the gesture, M4 the
+monotone verification chronometer); the attribution kit is deliberately
+minimal --- its judge is the model written for stateful terrains (the
+screen metrics posed by construction, the import guichet fail-closed
+through the import table, the leaf bound at its slot, the liaison
+verbatim at its arity).
